 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook 5b — DINOv3 + DinoTXT Zero-Shot Verb Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook performs zero-shot verb prediction on YouCook2 using **DINOv3** as the vision\n",
    "backbone, aligned with the **DinoTXT** text tower — a direct parallel to the DINOv2 DinoTXT\n",
    "notebook (NB5) for controlled backbone comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach (identical to DINOv2 notebook):**\n",
    "- Extract per-frame embeddings from each video segment using the frozen DINOv3 vision backbone\n",
    "- Temporally pool frame embeddings into a single video-level representation\n",
    "- For each segment, fill the `[MASK]` slot in the masked caption with every verb in the vocabulary\n",
    "- Encode all candidates with the frozen DinoTXT text tower\n",
    "- Pick the verb whose text embedding is most similar (cosine) to the video embedding\n",
    "- No training — purely zero-shot similarity in the shared vision-language space\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key difference from DINOv2 notebook:**\n",
    "- Vision backbone is DINOv3 ViT-L/16 instead of DINOv2 ViT-L/14\n",
    "- DinoTXT text tower is loaded from the DINOv3 repo (same architecture, re-trained on DINOv3 features)\n",
    "- Frame preprocessing uses DINOv3's image transforms (patch size 16, different normalisation)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reads:**\n",
    "- `annotations/segments_verbs_timed.csv` — captions, verbs, segment IDs\n",
    "- Raw video files (to extract frames on the fly) OR precomputed DINOv3 embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "**Produces:**\n",
    "- Top-1 and Top-5 verb prediction accuracy on the validation set\n",
    "- `processed/nb5b_dinov3_dinotxt_zeroshot_results.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:**\n",
    "1. DINOv3 repo cloned: `git clone https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3.git`\n",
    "2. DINOv3 ViT-L/16 backbone weights downloaded (requires HuggingFace license approval)\n",
    "3. DINOv3 DinoTXT text tower weights downloaded (same approval email includes both)"
   ]
  },
  {
