   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "load-model-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load DINOv3 + DinoTXT model (fully frozen)\n",
    "\n",
    "This uses `torch.hub.load` from the local DINOv3 repo clone, passing both the\n",
    "DinoTXT text tower weights and the DINOv3 backbone weights separately.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model architecture is identical to DINOv2 DinoTXT — same shared embedding\n",
    "dimension (1280), same text tower size — but the vision head was trained to align\n",
    "specifically with DINOv3 features rather than DINOv2 features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "load-model",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loading DINOv3 + DinoTXT...\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Model loaded: 866.6M parameters, 0 trainable (must be 0)\n",
      "All parameters frozen ✓\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Add DINOv3 repo to path so its internal imports resolve\n",
    "if DINOV3_REPO not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, DINOV3_REPO)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Loading DINOv3 + DinoTXT...\")\n",
    "dinotxt, tokenizer = torch.hub.load(\n",
    "    DINOV3_REPO,\n",
    "    'dinov3_vitl16_dinotxt_tet1280d20h24l',\n",
    "    source='local',\n",
    "    weights=DINOV3_DINOTXT_WEIGHTS,\n",
    "    backbone_weights=DINOV3_BACKBONE_WEIGHTS,\n",
    ")\n",
    "dinotxt = dinotxt.to(DEVICE).eval()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Freeze all parameters — this is zero-shot, nothing trains\n",
    "for p in dinotxt.parameters():\n",
    "    p.requires_grad = False\n",
    "\n",
    "total     = sum(p.numel() for p in dinotxt.parameters())\n",
    "trainable = sum(p.numel() for p in dinotxt.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\n",
    "print(f\"Model loaded: {total/1e6:.1f}M parameters, {trainable} trainable (must be 0)\")\n",
    "assert trainable == 0, \"Model must be fully frozen\"\n",
    "print(\"All parameters frozen ✓\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "transforms-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Image preprocessing transforms\n",
    "\n",
    "DINOv3 uses patch size 16 (vs DINOv2's patch size 14) and different normalisation\n",
    "statistics for LVD-1689M pretrained models. We use DINOv3's built-in transform."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "transforms",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from dinov3.data.transforms import make_classification_eval_transform\n",
    "\n",
    "# DINOv3 standard eval transform — 224x224 centre crop, ImageNet normalisation\n",
    "image_transform = make_classification_eval_transform(resize_size=256, crop_size=224)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Image transform ready ✓\")\n",
    "print(\"  resize_size : 256\")\n",
    "print(\"  crop_size   : 224\")\n",
    "print(\"  normalisation: DINOv3 LVD-1689M (ImageNet stats)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "extract-embeddings-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Extract and save DINOv3 video embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "For each video segment, we:\n",
    "1. Load the raw video frames for that segment\n",
    "2. Preprocess each frame with the DINOv3 transform\n",
    "3. Run frames through `dinotxt.encode_image()` in sub-batches\n",
    "4. Mean-pool frame embeddings → single segment embedding\n",
    "5. Save to `embeddings/dinov3/{segment_id}.pt`\n",
    "\n",
    "This is identical to what NB4 did for DINOv2, just using the DINOv3 vision tower.\n",
    "Skip this cell if embeddings are already computed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "extract-embeddings",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "0b3eb6e1b1134e45954f44cb5979d0ea",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "Extracting DINOv3 embeddings:   0%|          | 0/13029 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Embeddings saved : 13,003\n",
      "Skipped (exist)  : 13,003\n",
      "Errors           : 26\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import cv2\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "\n",
    "FRAME_BATCH_SIZE = 32   # sub-batch size for GPU memory safety on A100\n",
    "FRAMES_PER_SEG   = 16   # how many frames to sample per segment (consistent with DINOv2 NB4)\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_frames_for_segment(video_path: str, start_sec: float, end_sec: float, n_frames: int = FRAMES_PER_SEG):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract n_frames uniformly from a video segment [start_sec, end_sec].\"\"\"\n",
    "    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(video_path)\n",
    "    fps = cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FPS)\n",
    "    start_frame = int(start_sec * fps)\n",
    "    end_frame   = int(end_sec   * fps)\n",
    "    frame_indices = np.linspace(start_frame, end_frame - 1, n_frames, dtype=int)\n",
    "\n",
    "    frames = []\n",
    "    for idx in frame_indices:\n",
    "        cap.set(cv2.CAP_PROP_POS_FRAMES, idx)\n",
    "        ret, frame = cap.read()\n",
    "        if ret:\n",
    "            frame_rgb = cv2.cvtColor(frame, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n",
    "            frames.append(Image.fromarray(frame_rgb))\n",
    "    cap.release()\n",
    "    return frames\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@torch.no_grad()\n",
    "def embed_segment_dinov3(video_path: str, start_sec: float, end_sec: float) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract DINOv3 embedding for a video segment. Returns (1280,) L2-normalised.\"\"\"\n",
    "    frames = extract_frames_for_segment(video_path, start_sec, end_sec)\n",
    "    if len(frames) == 0:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "    frame_tensors = torch.stack([image_transform(f) for f in frames])  # (N, 3, 224, 224)\n",
    "\n",
    "    all_embeddings = []\n",
    "    with torch.autocast('cuda', dtype=torch.float):\n",
    "        for i in range(0, len(frame_tensors), FRAME_BATCH_SIZE):\n",
    "            batch = frame_tensors[i:i + FRAME_BATCH_SIZE].to(DEVICE)\n",
    "            emb   = dinotxt.encode_image(batch)  # (B, 1280)\n",
    "            all_embeddings.append(emb.cpu())\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Temporal mean pooling across frames\n",
    "    video_emb = torch.cat(all_embeddings, dim=0).mean(dim=0)  # (1280,)\n",
    "    video_emb = video_emb / video_emb.norm()                  # L2 normalise\n",
    "    return video_emb\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run extraction — skip segments that already have embeddings saved\n",
    "VIDEO_DIR = PATHS['videos']\n",
    "skipped = 0\n",
    "errors  = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "for _, row in tqdm(df.iterrows(), total=len(df), desc=\"Extracting DINOv3 embeddings\"):\n",
    "    out_path = os.path.join(DINOV3_EMB_DIR, f\"{row['segment_id']}.pt\")\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(out_path):\n",
    "        skipped += 1\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    video_path = os.path.join(VIDEO_DIR, f\"{row['video_id']}.mp4\")\n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(video_path):\n",
    "        errors += 1\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        emb = embed_segment_dinov3(video_path, row['start_time'], row['end_time'])\n",
    "        if emb is not None:\n",
    "            torch.save(emb, out_path)\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        errors += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "saved = len([f for f in os.listdir(DINOV3_EMB_DIR) if f.endswith('.pt')])\n",
    "print(f\"Embeddings saved : {saved:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Skipped (exist)  : {skipped:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Errors           : {errors:,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "text-embed-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Precompute verb text embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Identical to the DINOv2 DinoTXT notebook — for each segment we fill `[MASK]` with\n",
    "every verb in the vocabulary using that segment's actual masked caption context,\n",
    "then encode with the DinoTXT text tower.\n",
    "\n",
    "The text tower architecture and shared embedding dimension (1280) are the same\n",
    "between DINOv2-DinoTXT and DINOv3-DinoTXT, so this function is directly comparable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "text-embed",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Test caption          : [MASK] and chop the garlic\n",
      "Text embeddings shape : torch.Size([282, 2048])  (expected: (282, 1280))\n",
      "L2 norm               : 1.0000  (expected: ~1.0)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "CONTEXT_LENGTH = 77  # CLIP tokenizer max length\n",
    "\n",
    "@torch.no_grad()\n",
    "def get_text_embeddings_for_segment(masked_caption: str) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Given a masked caption like '[MASK] the onions into small pieces',\n",
    "    replace [MASK] with every verb in vocab and encode all candidates.\n",
    "    Returns tensor of shape (n_verbs, 1280), L2-normalised.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    caption_context = masked_caption.replace('[MASK]', '{}')\n",
    "    verb_texts      = [caption_context.format(v) for v in verb_vocab]\n",
    "\n",
    "    with torch.autocast('cuda', dtype=torch.float):\n",
    "        tokens        = tokenizer.tokenize(verb_texts).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "        text_features = dinotxt.encode_text(tokens)           # (n_verbs, 1280)\n",
    "    text_features = text_features / text_features.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n",
    "    return text_features\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick sanity check\n",
    "test_caption = df['masked_caption'].iloc[0]\n",
    "test_emb     = get_text_embeddings_for_segment(test_caption)\n",
    "print(f\"Test caption          : {test_caption}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Text embeddings shape : {test_emb.shape}  (expected: ({n_verbs}, 1280))\")\n",
    "print(f\"L2 norm               : {test_emb.norm(dim=-1).mean():.4f}  (expected: ~1.0)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "zeroshot-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Zero-shot verb prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "For each segment:\n",
    "1. Load the precomputed DINOv3 video embedding\n",
    "2. Encode all verb candidates in the caption context using DinoTXT text tower\n",
    "3. Pick the verb with highest cosine similarity to the video embedding\n",
    "4. Record Top-1 and Top-5 correctness\n",
    "\n",
    "This loop is **identical** to the DINOv2 DinoTXT notebook — only the embedding\n",
    "directory changes, making results directly comparable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "818bc135",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Train : 9,742\n",
      "Val   : 3,287\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('/home/ubuntu/youcook2-videos/annotations/segments_verbs_timed.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "verb_vocab = sorted(df['extracted_verb'].unique())\n",
    "label2id   = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(verb_vocab)}\n",
    "id2label   = {i: v for v, i in label2id.items()}\n",
    "n_verbs    = len(verb_vocab)\n",
    "df['verb_label'] = df['extracted_verb'].map(label2id)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_train = df[df['subset'] == 'training'].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "df_val   = df[df['subset'] == 'validation'].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train : {len(df_train):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Val   : {len(df_val):,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "cbf13188",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "8565b7e5a14748e08365f2d25f6d046c",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "Zero-shot prediction:   0%|          | 0/500 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Sample             : 500 val segments\n",
      "Predicted          : 500\n",
      "Missing embeddings : 0\n",
      "\n",
      "Val Top-1          : 0.0360  (3.60%)\n",
      "Val Top-5          : 0.1400  (14.00%)\n",
      "Random baseline    : 0.0035  (0.35%)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "results = []\n",
    "missing = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Only run on first 500 val segments\n",
    "df_sample = df_val.head(500)\n",
    "\n",
    "for _, row in tqdm(df_sample.iterrows(), total=len(df_sample), desc=\"Zero-shot prediction\"):\n",
    "    emb_path = os.path.join(DINOV3_EMB_DIR, f\"{row['segment_id']}.pt\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(emb_path):\n",
    "        missing += 1\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    video_emb = torch.load(emb_path, map_location=DEVICE)  # (1280,)\n",
    "    video_emb = video_emb / video_emb.norm()\n",
    "\n",
    "    text_embs = get_text_embeddings_for_segment(row['masked_caption'])  # (n_verbs, 1280)\n",
    "\n",
    "    similarity   = text_embs @ video_emb\n",
    "    top5_indices = similarity.topk(5).indices.tolist()\n",
    "    top1_verb    = verb_vocab[top5_indices[0]]\n",
    "    ground_truth = row['extracted_verb']\n",
    "    gt_idx       = verb_vocab.index(ground_truth) if ground_truth in verb_vocab else -1\n",
    "\n",
    "    results.append({\n",
    "        'segment_id'    : row['segment_id'],\n",
